## Developer API & Documentation

- [Meshy API Overview](https://www.meshy.ai/api): Integrate AI-powered 3D generation into your applications with the Meshy API. RESTful endpoints for Text-to-3D, Image-to-3D, texturing, and animation. SDKs available for Python, JavaScript, and Unity.
- [API Documentation](https://docs.meshy.ai/en): Complete API reference documentation with code examples, authentication guides, and endpoint specifications. Learn how to generate 3D models programmatically with detailed tutorials.
- [Text-to-3D API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#text-to-3d-beta): Generate 3D models from text descriptions via API. Supports style parameters, topology options, and quality settings. Returns downloadable 3D files in multiple formats.
- [Image-to-3D API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#image-to-3d): Convert images to 3D models programmatically. Upload single or multiple reference images. Supports PNG, JPG, and WebP input formats.
- [Multi-Image-to-3D API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#multi-image-to-3d-beta): Generate 3D models from multiple reference images for improved accuracy. Upload front, side, and back views for better geometry reconstruction.
- [Remesh API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#remesh-beta): Optimize and retopologize 3D meshes via API. Reduce polygon count while preserving detail. Prepare models for real-time applications.
- [Rigging & Animation API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#rigging-animation-beta): Auto-rig characters and apply animations programmatically. Choose from 600+ motion presets. Export rigged and animated models in FBX format.
- [Retexture API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#ai-texturing-beta): Apply AI-generated textures to existing 3D models via API. Supports text prompts and reference images for texture generation.
- [Text-to-Image API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#text-to-image-beta): Generate AI images optimized for 3D conversion. Create concept art, reference images, and multi-view renders for Image-to-3D workflows.
- [Image-to-Image API](https://docs.meshy.ai/#image-to-image-beta): Transform and enhance images for 3D generation. Style transfer, upscaling, and multi-view generation for improved 3D model quality.

